#{[17592186407247 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186407241 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186407247 #edb/ref 1069 "q-109861" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186407247 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186407247 #edb/ref 1071 "Let $A$ and $B$ be $m\\times p$ and $p\\times n$ matrices, respectively. What is the image of $\\text{Col}({B}^{T}\\,{A}^{T})$ under the action of $AB?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186407247 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "de769de3-3ab7-5536-ae28-2dcbd744b48f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186407247 #edb/ref 1074 "Pre-multiplying a vector $x\\in {R}^{n}$ by $AB$ gives a linear combination of the columns of $AB:$\n\n$$\n{{[\\begin{aligned}| & | & ⋯ & | \\\\ (ab)_{1} & (ab)_{2} & ⋯ & (ab)_{n} \\\\ | & | & ⋯ & |\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{AB}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {x}_{n}\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{x}={x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}| \\\\ (ab)_{1} \\\\ |\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}| \\\\ (ab)_{2} \\\\ |\\end{aligned}]+⋯+{x}_{n}[\\begin{aligned}| \\\\ (ab)_{n} \\\\ |\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nTherefore, the image of ${R}^{n}$ under the action of $AB$ must be $\\text{Col}(AB),$ the column space of $AB.$\n\nFurthermore, since $\\text{Null}(AB)$ is mapped to the zero vector $0$ by the definition of the null subspace, the image of its orthogonal complement $\\text{Col}((AB)^{T})=\\text{Col}({B}^{T}\\,{A}^{T})$ must be $\\text{Col}(AB).$\n\nThis can be schematically visualized, as shown below.\n\n![](images/88/885bf8a3061f93ad400897a7273ffe4157d22dee20b8e4ee7ebb982b1c4319bb.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186407248 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186407250 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186407248 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "453b68d4-1d9d-50c9-a90c-51c8b99946a5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186407248 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186407246 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186407249 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186407252 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186407249 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "6ef8f97d-5b2a-5ab0-998f-92729ef9dc31" #edb/r