 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186476411 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186476860 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186476464 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186476860 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186476570 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186476860 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186476860 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186476860 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186476344 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186476860 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "eeeef6de-d8de-527e-81b4-5538bfa583c5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186476861 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186476243 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186476861 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186476316 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186476861 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186476636 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186476861 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186476652 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186476861 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186476709 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186476861 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186476861 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186476861 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186476316 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186476861 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "ef854973-f40e-54d0-8398-b5ed45b6afdd" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186476871 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186476769 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186476871 #edb/ref 1069 "q-109872" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186476871 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186476871 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider a $7\\times 8$ matrix $A.$ If $\\text{dim}(\\text{Col}(A))=4,$ then $\\text{dim}(\\text{Null}(A))=$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186476871 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "0027448d-1eb1-5ed1-bd4f-f6f90763ed8e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186476871 #edb/ref 1074 "The four fundamental subspaces of a matrix $A$ can be schematically visualized, as shown below.\n\n![](images/88/889b83fadd26b377c4dd34143c9b16541630c04e90de3d9b005e7147ead75ad5.png)\n\nIn our case, we are given that $m=7,$ $n=8,$ and $r=4.$ \n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{dim}(\\text{Null}(A)) & =n-r=8-4=4.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186476888 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186476861 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186476888 #edb/ref 1069 "q-109856" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186476888 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186476888 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following subspaces must be orthogonal to $\\text{Null}(A+B)$ for all compatible matrices $A$ and $B?$\n\nI. $\\text{Null}({A}^{T}+{B}^{T})$\n\nII. $\\text{Col}({A}^{T}+{B}^{T})$\n\nIII. $\\text{Col}(A+B)$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186476888 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "3930016a-7426-5deb-b0f0-c2074d3a1ffd" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186476888 #edb/ref 1074 "Recall that $\\text{Null}(A+B)$ contains all vectors that, when pre-multiplied by $A+B,$ result in the zero-vector $0.$ \n\nWhen pre-multiplying a vector by $A+B,$ we actually multiply each row of $A+B$ by that vector. So, $\\text{Null}(A+B)$ must be orthogonal to the row space of $A+B,$ which is $\\text{Col}((A+B)^{T})=\\text{Col}({A}^{T}+{B}^{T}).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"\n\n**Note:** In general, the four fundamental subspaces of a matrix $A$ can be schematically visualized, as shown below.\n\n![](images/de/de22dd5b352e1d5be48f4b6ed3b2a4657ae623c1bd288d3464559758ea334af7.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186476895 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186476778 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186476895 #edb/ref 1069 "q-109857" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186476895 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186476895 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following subspaces must be orthogonal to $\\text{Null}({X}^{T}{Y}^{T})$ for all compatible matrices $X$ and $Y?$\n\nI. $\\text{Null}(YX)$\n\nII. $\\text{Col}({X}^{T}{Y}^{T})$\n\nIII. $\\text{Col}(YX)$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186476895 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "4d68ce86-72b3-53d7-b424-c8c3717fc180" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186476895 #edb/ref 1074 "Recall that $\\text{Null}({X}^{T}{Y}^{T})$ contains all vectors that, when pre-multiplied by ${X}^{T}{Y}^{T},$ result in the zero-vector $0.$ \n\nWhen pre-multiplying a vector by ${X}^{T}{Y}^{T},$ we actually multiply each row of ${X}^{T}{Y}^{T}$ by that vector. So, $\\text{Null}({X}^{T}{Y}^{T})$ must be orthogonal to the row space of ${X}^{T}{Y}^{T},$ which is $\\text{Col}(({X}^{T}{Y}^{T})^{T})=\\text{Col}(YX).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\"\n\n**Note:** In general, the four fundamental subspaces of a matrix $A$ can be schematically visualized, as shown below.\n\n![](images/de/de22dd5b352e1d5be48f4b6ed3b2a4657ae623c1bd288d3464559758ea334af7.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186476920 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186476860 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186476920 #edb/ref 1069 "q-109863" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186476920 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186476920 #edb/ref 1071 "Let $A$ and $B$ be $m\\times n$ matrices. What is the image of ${R}^{m}$ under the action of ${A}^{T}+{B}^{T}?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186476920 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "814b73ba-57d5-52a9-8c36-0c9f156faa4a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186476920 #edb/ref 1074 "First, notice that ${A}^{T}+{B}^{T}$ is a $n\\times m$ matrix.\n\nNow, pre-multiplying a vector $x\\in {R}^{m}$ by ${A}^{T}+{B}^{T}$ gives a linear combination of the columns of ${A}^{T}+{B}^{T}:$\n\n$$\n{{[\\begin{aligned}| & | & ⋯ & | \\\\ ({a}^{T}+{b}^{T})_{1} & ({a}^{T}+{b}^{T})_{2} & ⋯ & ({a}^{T}+{b}^{T})_{m} \\\\ | & | & ⋯ & |\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{A}^{T}+{B}^{T}}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {x}_{m}\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{x}={x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}| \\\\ ({a}^{T}+{b}^{T})_{1} \\\\ |\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}| \\\\ ({a}^{T}+{b}^{T})_{2} \\\\ |\\end{aligned}]+⋯+{x}_{m}[\\begin{aligned}| \\\\ ({a}^{T}+{b}^{T})_{m} \\\\ |\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nTherefore, the image of ${R}^{m}$ under the action of ${A}^{T}+{B}^{T}$ must be $\\text{Col}({A}^{T}+{B}^{T}),$ the row space of $A+B.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186476953 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186476777 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186476953 #edb/ref 1069 "q-108924" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186476953 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186476953 #edb/ref 1071 "Let $A$ be a $m\\times n$ matrix. What is the image of $\\text{Null}({A}^{T})$ under the action of ${A}^{T}?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186476953 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "bb821d7a-e914-5964-b025-342c273fea77" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186476953 #edb/ref 1074 "By definition of the null subspace, $\\text{Null}({A}^{T})$ is mapped to the zero vector $0$ under the action of ${A}^{T}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
